OL,3,GNEWSAThe volunteers 'preserving the
OL,4,Apast' at the side of the road
OL,5,
OL,6,FOnce a common sight at the side of
OL,7,FBritish roads, with more than 600
OL,8,Fconstructed between 1911 and 1962, AA
OL,9,Ftelephone boxes are now a rarity.
OL,11,FOnly a handful remain in their original
OL,12,Flocations, where they once provided
OL,13,Frefuge for the breakdown service's
OL,14,Fpatrols, storage for water and fuel and
OL,15,Fa telephone back to base.
OL,17,FMembers of the Automobile Association
OL,18,F(AA) were also given access to the
OL,19,Fboxes from 1919 onwards, to allow them
OL,20,Fto call for assistance, with around two
OL,21,Fmillions keys issued over the folloiwng
OL,22,F80 years.
OL,23,APub: 10-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
